WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:04.930
To some of you have rightly and accurately
pointed out to me that suddenly Florida's

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:10.010
corona virus cases have started to decline,
California's corona virus cases don't seem

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.559
to be spiking the way the trajectory suggested.

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:14.650
And I started to look into this.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.710
And indeed, it is true.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:20.650
If you look at Florida, their cases have started
to drop off.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:24.679
But it just so happens that Florida stopped
testing.

00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:26.179
This is no conspiracy theory.

00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:30.830
This is what they announced they were going
to do because of the hurricane.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.379
Hurricane SARS.

00:00:32.379 --> 00:00:36.859
As Donald Trump has struggled to say, look
at this article from NPR from July twenty

00:00:36.859 --> 00:00:39.780
ninth saying Florida will pause.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.809
Corona virus testing due to impending storm.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:45.220
Now, it didn't happen all at once.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.469
In all of the counties.

00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:49.589
So we are still seeing thousands of cases
a day from Florida.

00:00:49.589 --> 00:00:54.180
But because different counties, as the hurricane
worked its way through the state, stopped

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.280
testing, the numbers of tests went down dramatically.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.250
And we can sort of turn to Donald Trump's
favorite phrase here.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.440
If you don't test, you don't find cases.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.690
And that's true.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:10.650
The article saying, quote, After the state's
testing sites close Thursday evening, that's

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:15.500
last Thursday, they won't reopen until at
least Tuesday morning.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.730
That's yesterday.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:22.460
That's according to Candi Simms of the Florida
Department of Health in Broward County.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:23.860
So what do we do?

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:27.190
Well, one thing we can look at is ICU usage.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:33.470
And you can see that Florida ICU usage hit
100 percent in the last week of July and it's

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:34.750
still there.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.330
You can actually go over 100 percent in that.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:42.520
You can start to convert non ICU spaces in
hospitals to temporary ICU.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.740
But Florida has been stuck at 100 percent
ICU usage for days.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.130
This is very, very bad.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:54.610
And I'm getting more and more people saying,
can we even trust the numbers now?

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.390
Can we trust the case numbers?

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:59.450
Can we even trust the death numbers right
now?

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.040
And this is a real concern.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:07.340
Now, part of the concern generally comes from
the change that happened from July 15th into

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:12.750
July 16th, where hospitals were mandated to
stop reporting directly to the CDC and instead

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.440
to the Department of Health and Human Services.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:22.740
There are open questions as to if and to what
degree that has influenced numbers in specific

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.130
states, though we know why the case numbers
are going down.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:27.710
Florida is one example.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:31.090
They stopped testing because of the hurricane.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.210
Let's look at California.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:39.090
California now is admitting that for days
they've been underreporting case numbers.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.170
The explanation is still not totally clear.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:44.600
And maybe by later today or tomorrow, we will
know more about it.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:49.750
But a message appeared on California's COBA
19 dashboard, which said, quote, Due to the

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:56.010
issues with the state's electronic laboratory
system, these data represent an underreporting

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:58.440
of actual positive cases.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:04.020
California's top health official, Dr. Mark
Gallie, said, quote, Over the past few days,

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:07.050
the state system, we've discovered some discrepancies.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.060
So we're still waiting on more information.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.700
But when you look at the globe, the national
case numbers, and you see that they seem to

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.120
at least have stopped increasing.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:22.420
Understand that two of the major case centers,
Florida and California, are underreporting

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.420
cases.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.420
One, because they are there.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.270
They've stopped testing because of a weather
event.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:29.240
California for some unknown reason that they've
discovered discrepancies.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:35.810
And yet, even with Florida reducing testing,
even with California underreporting, we still

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.360
at 54000 new cases yesterday.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.220
We still had almost 49000 new cases on Monday.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.830
So a few different thoughts on this.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.709
Cases aren't really declining.

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:48.460
They've kind of leveled off at the national
level.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:51.000
But two states are underreporting.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.740
And that would be a huge piece of why that
is.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:59.190
So first off, at this point, it's very hard
to say for sure whether cases are still growing

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:02.330
nationally or have leveled off or what's going
on.

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:06.090
What we do know is that the big picture, the
sort of fundamentals of what's happening in

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.170
the country haven't really changed.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:12.360
So we wouldn't really expect a huge decline
because there haven't been any big changes

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:13.360
in policy.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:19.069
Now, it's conceivable that even without states
really changing policy, that people are seeing

00:04:19.069 --> 00:04:21.909
the headlines and they're being more cautious.

00:04:21.909 --> 00:04:22.909
That's possible.

00:04:22.909 --> 00:04:27.069
It would take about fifteen or so days to
notice that.

00:04:27.069 --> 00:04:31.580
And increasingly, deaths are going to be the
indicator to the extent that we can trust

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.580
them.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:36.099
And if you look at the trend line in terms
of deaths, the seven day moving average, which

00:04:36.099 --> 00:04:41.979
sort of smooths out those dips of reporting
that happen over the weekend, the death rate

00:04:41.979 --> 00:04:44.870
rate than the death trends don't look good.

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:49.009
They may have maybe leveled off slightly,
but yesterday, again, we had nearly 15 hundred

00:04:49.009 --> 00:04:50.009
deaths.

00:04:50.009 --> 00:04:51.680
So it's too early to say.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.319
And then you get to are there ways to cover
up deaths?

00:04:55.319 --> 00:04:59.139
We know that there are you can mess with cause
of death.

00:04:59.139 --> 00:05:00.779
You can do other other things.

00:05:00.779 --> 00:05:08.189
So the important message, I think, is we're
in an area now where there is a question mark

00:05:08.189 --> 00:05:09.930
around the accuracy of the data.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.460
We don't have to go conspiratorial.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:13.089
We don't have to make any definitive statements.

00:05:13.089 --> 00:05:17.130
We can just say there are reasons to be skeptical
of the data.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:21.289
Including that Florida stop testing in California
is underreporting.

00:05:21.289 --> 00:05:27.660
So we are still at huge risk of even bigger
spikes when the United States got from, what

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:31.910
was it, 35000 cases a day, down to 20000.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:36.680
Almost every state started reopening 20000
cases we still had, and many states saw that

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.220
as a license to open.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:43.620
And we got all the way back up to 70000 cases
a day at one point about ten days ago.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:50.089
What we can say for sure is widespread reopening
and ignoring risk factors and risky activities

00:05:50.089 --> 00:05:54.589
and not wearing masks is going to create a
completely out of control spike.

00:05:54.589 --> 00:05:57.259
And just look at some of the headlines from
the last 24 hours.

00:05:57.259 --> 00:06:00.559
Teachers returned to a Georgia school district
last week.

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:04.669
260 employees have already gone home to quarantine.

00:06:04.669 --> 00:06:05.669
Not good.

00:06:05.669 --> 00:06:11.910
Dr. Foushee says if we don't get below 10000
cases a day before the fall, we will have

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.699
an even more insane explosion in the fall.

00:06:14.699 --> 00:06:16.840
And that's still 10000 cases a day.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:21.620
That would mean we need is like an 80 to 90
percent reduction to get down to 10000 cases

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:22.740
a day.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:30.960
Clorox announces it will not have enough disinfecting
wipes until 2021, according to its CEO.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:37.360
Twenty five people have been infected at a
Bible camp in Oregon when Corona virus subsided

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:38.360
in Israel.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:39.990
Israel reopened schools.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:43.139
It didn't go well and things are shutting
back down.

00:06:43.139 --> 00:06:44.279
This is a real thing.

00:06:44.279 --> 00:06:47.270
You know, when Trump says it's the invisible
enemy.

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:48.270
It's this dumb thing.

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:52.259
He keeps repeating the invisible scorch, nobody
telling him it's pronounced scourge.

00:06:52.259 --> 00:06:57.839
OK, but in a sense, it can feel as though
it's not really there because it is invisible.

00:06:57.839 --> 00:07:00.050
We see the results through our actions.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:04.620
Our actions directly impact these numbers
to the extent that we get the real numbers.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:05.930
And we need to be very cautious.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:10.759
You know, I'm trying to take it in stride
in the sense that my I can only focus on my

00:07:10.759 --> 00:07:11.849
sphere of influence.

00:07:11.849 --> 00:07:13.729
I can't control what everybody in the country
does.

00:07:13.729 --> 00:07:15.330
I can't control what the policy is.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:18.589
I can ensure that I'm acting as responsibly
as possible.

00:07:18.589 --> 00:07:22.669
And at least to you, I communicate what seems
to be responsible.

00:07:22.669 --> 00:07:24.460
Our actions have consequences.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:08:06.990
And if it's I can't think of a time where
it's been more clear than it is

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:46.790
right now.

